  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: b470753b54ce932469c2c759655f968e, type: 3}
  m_Name: Notebook
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::CatchableItem
  itemName: Notebook
  modelPrefab: {fileID: 5960034880092928018, guid: 152a90e593889c741afc7c3418320489, type: 3}
  dialogueLines:
  - A notebook... and it's totally dry? Something is wrong here. Maybe there's something
    in it that explains it.
  - '"To whom it may concern." Any note that starts like that can''t be good.'
  - '"There was once a town here. A thriving, joyful town, with all kinds of people
    filling it''s streets."'
  - '"As I''m sure you can tell, something happened. Something that, as I''m writing
    this, I''m doing everything I can to prevent, but I fear the worst may come to
    pass."'
  - '"This town is soon to be swallowed up by water entirely. What will happen to
    me, and the other inhabitants, I''m not sure. But I hope that whoever reads this
    will remember."'
  - '"Remember that this place used to be a home. A home that, hopefully, could one
    day be restored. '
  - 'This is a lot to take in... is this why I''ve had this sense of familiarity? '
  - Maybe... this town under the lake was once... my home?
